            "review_title": "Review at Cay De Vegetarian Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Docs On Vacay\nMalaysia3234 contributions\n7\nThe Best Vegetarian Restaurant in the entire 3 days I spent in HCMC\nMar 2020\n🍃To be on the safe side, Michelle and I opted for vegetarian cuisine, since we don't at all eat pork. Apparently, HCMC has an abundance of vegetarian restaurants! We walked to this restaurant named 'Cay De Vegetarian Restaurant', and it was perhaps the best meal we ever had in HCMC! The vegetarian soup noodles were spicy and rich! They had so many authentic Vietnamese dishes, we were spoilt for choice. Just take a look at the photos. Vietnamese tend to use the freshest leaves in almost every dish serve; basil leaves, cilantro, etc. Pickles, chilies and lime is always served as a side to complement the main dish. And the Vietnamese spring rolls, crisp and hot from the wok, were too good describe, especially we were both famished when we arrived.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 7, 2021",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
