            "review_title": "Review at Cay De Vegetarian Restaurant",
            "review_text": "cieraturton\nLondon, United Kingdom12 contributions\n0\nTasty vegan meal\nJan 2020 • Family\nThere was plenty of choice here and the food was delicious. Very flavoursome (I’ve found some of the vegetarian restaurants can sometimes be a bit bland) and it did not disappoint. Pricing was very reasonable. The only problem was that, despite being a vegetarian/vegan restaurant, they decided to put a live fish in the table decoration. The fish was in a small vase and kept getting trapped in the roots of the plant in it. For a omnivore restaurant I would find this a bit distasteful but unsurprising, but for a vegetarian/vegan place I found it really odd. I would say to get rid of the live fish display and just have the plant! \n\nThat aside, this is a good place for food\nRead more\nWritten January 1, 2020",
